<section class="section">
  <div class="shell about-narrative">
    <p class="section-index">The story so far</p>
    <div class="story-chapter"><span>2017</span><div><h2>I started Upstack Studio.</h2><p>For years, my team and I built web and mobile products with business owners. I saw what customers needed, what teams could use and why some projects worked while others did not.</p><p>It taught me a simple lesson: the hard part is rarely the code. Knowing what to build matters more than knowing how to build it.</p></div></div>
    <figure class="wide-story-photo"><img src="/assets/images/adrian/upstack-team.webp" alt="Adrian Ching with the Upstack Studio team" loading="lazy" width="1130" height="1130"><figcaption>The Upstack Studio team.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="story-chapter"><span>Then</span><div><h2>I shut the agency down.</h2><p>I could have kept improving the model. But it was no longer the company I wanted to build. I wanted to own the products, own the results and focus on fewer, bigger ideas.</p><p>There was no grand ending. It was simply the right decision.</p></div></div>
    <div class="story-chapter"><span>Now</span><div><h2>AI changed the cost of building software.</h2><p>Software is getting faster and cheaper to make. Choosing the right problem is becoming more important than ever.</p><p>Small teams can now do much more. They can also waste money much faster. That is why I care so much about deciding what is worth doing before starting the work.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark" id="what-im-building">
  <div class="shell about-build-grid">
    <div><p class="section-index">What I’m building</p><h2>One main company.<br>One growing portfolio.</h2></div>
    <div class="build-ambition"><span>01</span><h3>Second Team</h3><p>Second Team is my main company. It gets most of my time and it is the company I’m building for the next decade.</p><p>I keep the product work private and share the lessons as I build.</p></div>
    <div class="build-ambition"><span>02</span><h3>My portfolio</h3><p>Alongside Second Team, I’m building a portfolio of software products, media and online businesses that I own and operate.</p><p>This website is where I share the work, including the parts that do not go to plan.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell values-grid">
    <div><p class="section-index">How I work</p><h2>A few rules I come back to.</h2></div>
    <div class="values-list"><p><span>01</span>Start with the business problem, not the tool.</p><p><span>02</span>Tell the truth, even when the answer is “do not build it.”</p><p><span>03</span>Do fewer things and give them proper attention.</p><p><span>04</span>Let AI handle repeatable work. Keep people on judgement and relationships.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

